  "readmeFile": "readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "BREAKING CHANGES:\n            - All static settings removed; every global setting now lives on TestSdkSettings:\n              HttpClientAssertExtensions.JsonSerializerOptions / SkipEndpointValidation / ShowTokenInCurl / LogAction,\n              AssertObjectExtensions.JsonSerializerOptions / DifferenceFunc / DifferenceFilter / OrderIndependentArrayFilter / WriteResponse\n              -> same names on TestSdkSettings.\n            - HttpClientAssertExtensions.CustomAssertableHttpClient removed: register your own IAssertableHttpClient before AddAssertableHttpClient.\n            - AssertObjectExtensions.ResponseFileFullPath removed (had no effect).\n            - Environment variable AspNetCoreSimpleMsTestSdk__WriteResponse renamed to TestSdkSettings__WriteResponse.\n            - Public helpers Tables.TableFormatter and Outputs.Formatters.JsonTypeMismatchFormatter removed.\n            Configure via services.AddTestSdkSettings(configuration, s => ...), services.AddAssertableHttpClient(configuration, s => ...)\n            or HttpClientAssertExtensions.Setup(s => ...) when there is no host.\n\n            NEW FEATURES:\n            - Output modes: TestSdkSettings.OutputMode = Human | Ai | Hybrid (env var TestSdkSettings__OutputMode=Ai) for structured, AI-parseable failures.\n            - HttpClientAssertExtensions.Setup(Action<TestSdkSettings>) for tests without a host.\n            - ApiTestBase<T> shares the running host's service provider with the assert extensions.\n\n            FIXES:\n            - Dictionary responses in recording mode (writeResponse) no longer fail with an array/object mismatch.\n\n            Full details: RELEASE-NOTES.md in the repository.",
